{% tool-context
   title="Load Predictor"
   question="What is load prediction?"
   definition="Load prediction turns recent demand, growth, recurring peaks, and known events into a planning range. The range matters more than a precise-looking point because traffic changes and model error can consume capacity before a scaling response is ready."
   inputs="Fit the historical signal with a baseline, trend, volatility, and measured backtest error. Then shape seasonality and events, set a tested serving envelope, and choose how much capacity to reserve."
   outcome="Compare expected and challenged demand with usable capacity. Use the first saturation day, peak shortfall, requests at risk, and required fleet size to define an alert and scaling action."
   experiment="Start with the expected range, then inject a launch spike, trend break, flash crowd, regional failover, and forecast error. Notice which failures increase demand and which remove capacity." /%}

